# UI & Styling — VTC Apps

## Tailwind CSS v4 — required on new apps

**New apps:** Tailwind **v4 only** — install `tailwindcss` + `@tailwindcss/postcss` + `postcss`. Do not scaffold v3 (`@tailwind` directives, `tailwindcss` PostCSS plugin, or v3-style `content` arrays).

**Legacy apps:** If the project already uses Tailwind v3, do not migrate to v4 unless the user asks — match the existing major version.

```javascript
// postcss.config.mjs or postcss.config.js — ONLY @tailwindcss/postcss
export default { plugins: { '@tailwindcss/postcss': {} } }
```

- ❌ Do NOT use `tailwindcss` as a PostCSS plugin
- ❌ Do NOT add `autoprefixer` (v4 handles prefixes)
- ❌ Do NOT use `@tailwind base|components|utilities`
- ❌ Do NOT use `prefers-color-scheme` / media-query dark mode
- `tailwind.config.ts` is **optional** in v4 — prefer CSS `@theme` below

```css
/* src/app/globals.css */
@import "tailwindcss" source(none);
@source "../**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}";

@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));
```

**Why `source(none)`:** Limit class scanning to `src/` only. Do not use bare `@import "tailwindcss"` — Tailwind v4 auto-scans the project root and may follow `.cursor/rules` symlinks, breaking Turbopack or slowing dev.

**Legacy v3 apps:** Keep `@tailwind base|components|utilities` — do not add `source(none)` on v3.

```css
/* @theme block — after @import / @source */
@theme {
  --color-surface-50: #f8fafc;
  --color-surface-200: #e2e8f0;
  --color-surface-300: #cbd5e1;
  --color-surface-500: #64748b;
  --color-surface-600: #475569;
  --color-surface-700: #334155;
  --color-surface-800: #1e293b;
  /* Runtime accent — map to CSS vars set by ThemeProvider */
  --color-app-accent: var(--app-accent);
  --color-app-accent-hover: var(--app-accent-hover);
  --color-app-accent-soft: var(--app-accent-soft);
  --color-app-accent-border: var(--app-accent-border);
  --color-app-accent-text: var(--app-accent-text);
}
```

```css
/* :root fallbacks only — ThemeProvider overwrites at runtime */
:root {
  --app-accent: #004a80;           /* VTC Blue — platform fallback */
  --app-accent-hover: #003a6e;
  --app-accent-soft: color-mix(in srgb, var(--app-accent) 14%, transparent);
  --app-accent-border: color-mix(in srgb, var(--app-accent) 35%, transparent);
  --app-accent-text: var(--app-accent);
}

/* Dark mode — accent hue is often too dark on surface-800; force readable accent text */
.dark {
  --app-accent-text: #ffffff;
}

@layer utilities {
  .dark .text-app-accent {
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .dark .text-app-accent-text {
    color: #ffffff;
  }
}
```

Use utilities `bg-surface-800`, `border-surface-200`, `bg-app-accent`, `text-app-accent`, `ring-app-accent`, etc. `ThemeProvider` sets `.dark` on `<html>` from URL `mode` (`light` | `dark`) and resolves accent tokens — see **Runtime Accent Color Standard** below.

**Dev watchers (EMFILE):** mandatory `next.config.ts` + Tailwind scoping — see **`dev-watch.mdc`** (do not duplicate here; always apply both).

## Next.js dev — ignore `.cursor` and parent dirs (v4 apps)

Use the full **`dev-watch.mdc`** `next.config.ts` block (`followSymlinks: false`, ignore parent suite folder, path guard). Minimal snippet is **not** sufficient for apps inside `eduslide/` or `crm_suite/`.

## Shared Cursor rules (local only)

After clone, link central rules — **never commit `.cursor/`**:

```bash
~/apps/cursor/scripts/add.sh my-app
# → .cursor/rules -> ~/apps/cursor/rules
```

Do not symlink the whole `~/apps/cursor` repo as `.cursor`.

## Dual theme — mandatory (new apps)

Every screen and shared component must work in **light and dark**:

- Pair backgrounds, borders, and text: `bg-white dark:bg-surface-800`, `text-gray-900 dark:text-white`, etc.
- Landing page, forms, errors, modals, nav — not only dashboard
- No hardcoded colors that only look correct in one mode
- Verify with `?mode=light` and `?mode=dark` (or toggle via `ThemeProvider`)

## Dark mode accent contrast — mandatory

Space accent colors are often **dark blues/purples**. In dark mode (`dark:bg-surface-800`), `text-app-accent` alone is **illegible** — the app name, pills, links, and badges disappear into the background.

**This is a common failure.** AI must apply **all** of the following — not only `dark:text-white` on the App Shell header.

### 1. `globals.css` (every app)

Include the `.dark { --app-accent-text: #ffffff }` block and `.dark .text-app-accent` utility override from the `@theme` / `:root` section above. Copy from **`~/apps/jobs`** if unsure.

### 2. `ThemeProvider` (every app)

When setting accent tokens on `document.documentElement`, **accent text must flip to white in dark mode**:

```ts
root.style.setProperty('--app-accent-text', mode === 'dark' ? '#ffffff' : accent)
```

Do **not** set `--app-accent-text` to the raw accent hue when `mode === 'dark'`.

### 3. `@vtc/ui` App Shell header

Use **`@vtc/ui@^1.1.2`** (or newer). `AppShell` renders the app name with `text-app-accent dark:text-white` when **standalone**. When **embedded in the platform shell iframe**, hide the in-app app name — platform chrome shows it (`Platform shell chrome`).

Prefer a **thin wrapper** around `VtcAppShell` from `@vtc/ui` — do not fork `AppShell.tsx` unless unavoidable.

### 4. Component class rules

| Use case | Class |
|----------|-------|
| Filled primary button | `bg-app-accent text-white` (unchanged) |
| Pills / badges on `bg-app-accent-soft` | `bg-app-accent-soft text-app-accent-text` — **not** `text-app-accent` alone |
| Links, labels, stats on dark surfaces | `text-app-accent-text` or `text-app-accent dark:text-white` |
| App Shell header app name | **Standalone only** — handled by `@vtc/ui` `AppShell` (`dark:text-white`). **Embedded:** omit — platform chrome |
| Hero / landing titles on dark bg | `text-app-accent dark:text-white` — see `landing-page.mdc` |

`text-app-accent` is for **light surfaces** and filled accent backgrounds. On `dark:bg-surface-800` (or any dark surface), always pair with `dark:text-white` or use `text-app-accent-text`.

### 5. Icons in dark mode (Heroicons, Lucide, emoji)

Icon libraries use **`currentColor`** for stroke/fill. They inherit the **text color** of the icon element or its parent.

| Pattern | Dark mode fix |
|---------|----------------|
| `<Icon className="w-6 h-6 text-app-accent" />` | Covered by `globals.css` `.dark .text-app-accent { color: #ffffff }` |
| Parent `div` with `text-app-accent`, child `<Icon />` | Child inherits white via `currentColor` |
| Preferred explicit pattern | `<Icon className="w-6 h-6 text-app-accent-text" />` inside `bg-app-accent-soft` box |
| Hardcoded `stroke="#004a80"` or `fill="var(--app-accent)"` on SVG | **Will not fix** — use `currentColor` + text utility classes |
| `<img>` icons | Unaffected — use filter or separate dark asset |

**Landing page feature cards** (`landing-page.mdc`): put `text-app-accent-text` on the icon, not only on the wrapper:

```tsx
<div className="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-app-accent-soft flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
  <FeatureIcon className="w-6 h-6 text-app-accent-text" aria-hidden />
</div>
```

### 6. Audit before shipping

1. Open `?mode=dark&color=%23004a80` (or the space's real accent).
2. Check: App Shell title, landing hero, benefit/tag pills, links, selected filter chips, avatar initials on soft accent bg.
3. Grep: `text-app-accent` — every hit on a dark surface needs `dark:text-white`, `text-app-accent-text`, or the mandatory `globals.css` dark overrides.
4. Check landing/feature **icons** in `?mode=dark` — must be white or high-contrast on `bg-app-accent-soft`.
5. Confirm `package-lock.json` resolves `@vtc/ui` ≥ `1.1.1` (or local `AppShell` has `dark:text-white` on the app name).

## Typography Standard (platform-wide — mandatory)

All in-house VTC apps follow the **same semantic roles** — see **`typography.mdc`** (caption, body, section, tab-primary, row-title, overlay-title, etc.). **Do not invent per-app scales.**

`ui.mdc` below covers **font family**, shell chrome, and component patterns. **Sizes and heading hierarchy** are defined only in `typography.mdc`.

### 1. Font family

- **Default:** platform system sans stack (`ui.mdc` / Tailwind `font-sans`).
- **Network policy:** when shell passes `typography=network` and optional `font=lato|system`, set `--app-font-family` on `<html>` via `ThemeProvider` + `themeFonts.ts` — see `network-branding.mdc`.
- **Do not** import custom fonts in individual apps unless `typography=network` (Lato loaded centrally).
- **Do not** use app-specific `font-family` classes that bypass `--app-font-family`.
- Type **sizes and weights** remain platform-standard in all modes.

### 2. Base text

- Body text: `text-sm` or `text-base` depending on density.
- **Default app UI body:** `text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300`
- Long reading content / articles may use `text-base` with comfortable line height (`leading-relaxed`).

```tsx
<main className="text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300">
  {/* page content */}
</main>
```

### 3. Header app name

Top bar app name only — never a screen title.

**Platform shell embed (default):** When the app runs inside the VTC shell iframe (`app.vtc.com` / `beta.vtc.com`), the **platform chrome bar** already shows the app title (including the space admin **display name** override). **Do not repeat the app name** in the child app's sticky header — header is **action slots only** (back when nested + slots 1–3 + ellipsis). See **Platform shell chrome** below.

**Standalone / direct URL** (rare — marketing, external open, dev without iframe): show app name in the sticky top bar:

```tsx
<h1 className="text-lg font-semibold text-app-accent dark:text-white truncate min-w-0">{appName}</h1>
```

- Long names must `truncate`. Matches **overlay-title** in `typography.mdc`.

### 4. Page / screen titles (in `<main>`)

**Embedded in platform shell:** do not use large page titles — the shell already shows context. Use **section** (`text-sm font-semibold`) for in-panel structure only.

**Standalone** (rare): if a screen needs a visible title, use **overlay-title**, not `text-2xl`:

```tsx
<h2 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{screenTitle}</h2>
```

### 5. Section headings

```tsx
<h3 className="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{sectionTitle}</h3>
```

Card groups, form sections, settings groups — **section** role in `typography.mdc`.

### 6. Card / list titles

**Compact** (default):

```tsx
<h4 className="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{itemTitle}</h4>
```

Do **not** use `text-base font-semibold` for default rows unless a deliberate feature card (still `text-sm` preferred).

### 7. Body / supporting text

```tsx
<p className="text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">{description}</p>
```

Use for descriptions, helper text, summaries, subtitles, and secondary copy.

### 8. Captions / metadata

```tsx
<span className="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">{timestamp}</span>
```

Use for timestamps, counts, labels, secondary metadata, and small hints.

### 9. Labels / tags / badges

```tsx
<span className="text-xs font-medium">{label}</span>
```

- **Uppercase** only for very short status labels (e.g. `NEW`, `VIP`) — `uppercase` + `tracking-wide` optional.
- **Avoid uppercase** for translated or longer labels.

### 10. Buttons

```tsx
<button className="text-sm font-medium ...">{label}</button>
```

- Standard button text: `text-sm font-medium`
- Primary action buttons may use `font-semibold` only when visually needed
- Icon-only buttons must have `aria-label` (and `title`) from i18n — no visible text

### 11. Line height

| Context | Class |
|---------|-------|
| Compact UI rows | `leading-tight` or `leading-snug` |
| Normal body / help text | `leading-relaxed` |
| Long-form article content | `prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert` |

### 12. Rules

- **Do not** create random text sizes in app code unless there is a clear layout reason.
- Prefer the defined scale: `text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg`, `text-xl`, `text-2xl`.
- **Avoid `text-3xl+`** inside apps except landing pages (`landing-page.mdc`), marketing pages, or empty-state hero screens.
- **Do not** use `font-light` or `font-black` in normal app UI.
- **Do not** use `text-app-accent` for large blocks of text — reserve for app name, selected states, links, and important accents.

### Quick reference

| Role | Classes |
|------|---------|
| Header app name (standalone only) | `text-xl font-bold text-app-accent dark:text-white truncate` |
| Page title (list / home) | `text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white` |
| Page title (nested / form) | `text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white` |
| Section heading | `text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white` |
| Card / list title | `text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white` |
| Body / supporting | `text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300` |
| Caption / metadata | `text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400` |
| Tag / badge | `text-xs font-medium` |
| Button | `text-sm font-medium` |

## App Shell — mandatory (all in-house VTC apps)

Every authenticated screen uses the **standard App Shell** — do not invent custom navigation (sidebars, tab bars, hamburger menus) unless the brief explicitly requires it.

| Zone | Rule |
|------|------|
| **Header** | Sticky top bar — `ui.mdc` header pattern below |
| **Body** | Centered responsive container — width by screen purpose (below) |
| **Actions** | **Header action slots** only — max 3 icons + vertical ellipsis; no bottom bar, no FAB — see below |
| **Text in top bar** | **Standalone:** app name (left). **Shell iframe embed:** **no app name** — platform chrome shows it; slots + back only. Also **no app-name home heading or subtitle** when embedded (§ Platform shell chrome) |

- Authenticated home = **task/list screen**, not a dashboard — `ux-screens.mdc`
- Admin/settings entry = **ellipsis menu** by default — never plain text links or labeled menus in the top bar

## Platform shell chrome — no app name anywhere when embedded (mandatory)

Child apps on `*.apps.vtc.com` open **inside the VTC shell iframe** (`app.vtc.com`, `beta.vtc.com`, desktop and mobile). The shell renders a **grey chrome bar** above the iframe with:

- Close (left)
- **App title centered** — space admin display name when set, else module name
- App tools / help (right)

The chrome is the **only** place the app name appears. When embedded, a child app must not show its own name **anywhere**:

| Surface | Embedded in shell | Standalone (direct tab, signed-out landing) |
|---------|-------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Sticky header (left) | `BackButton` when nested — **no app name** | `BackButton` when nested + app name |
| Home / root screen heading | **None** — no `<h1>`/`<h2>`/`pageTitle`/`PageTitle`/hero that says the app name | Unchanged |
| Home subtitle / tagline | **None** — no "Your personal X", "Welcome to X", "X for your Space", "Shared with this Space's team"-style lane captions | Unchanged |
| Nested screen titles (`backHref` set: "Library", "New post", …) | ✅ Keep — they name the **screen**, not the app | ✅ |
| Empty states / help copy that mention the app in a sentence | ✅ OK ("Connect an account to start posting") — avoid leading with the name | ✅ |
| Signed-out **landing page** / promo (`landing-page.mdc`) | Unchanged (hero may show the app name) | Unchanged |

**Home screen starts straight with content or actions** — stats, list, primary CTA, search. No title block above it. (`ux-screens.mdc`: authenticated home = task/list screen.)

### Use `@vtc/ui` ≥ 1.4.0 (default does the right thing)

`@vtc/ui` **1.4.0** `AppShell` hides `appName` **by default** when `isEmbeddedInShell()` is true, and drops a **root** `pageTitle` that equals the app name. Nested `pageTitle` (with `backHref`) always renders.

```tsx
// src/components/AppShell.tsx — thin wrapper (no embed logic needed with ui ≥ 1.4.0)
<VtcAppShell appName={displayName} addToken={addTokenToUrl} {...rest}>{children}</VtcAppShell>

// Home page — no pageTitle, no subtitle
<AppShell {...headerSlots(t)} overflow={overflow(t)}>
  <StatsRow … />
  <PrimaryCta … />
</AppShell>
```

- `hideAppName` prop: `undefined` = auto (hide when embedded) · `true` = always hide · `false` = always show (rare standalone-only surfaces).
- `isEmbeddedInShell()` / `useEmbeddedInShell()` (hydration-safe) are exported for app code that renders its **own** header or hero.
- `@vtc/ui` **< 1.4.0 has no `hideAppName` prop** — older versions of this rule referenced it before it shipped, so passing it did nothing. Upgrade: `npm install @vtc/ui@^1.4.0` (lockfile must resolve ≥ 1.4.0; CI uses `npm ci`).

### Custom headers (apps that don't use `@vtc/ui` AppShell)

```ts
import { useEmbeddedInShell } from '@vtc/ui' // or copy:
export function isEmbeddedInShell(): boolean {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return false
  try { return window.self !== window.top } catch { return true }
}
```

Any component that renders the app name (`t('app.name')`, `t('app.title')`, `APP_NAME`, env display name, literal) in a header, home heading or home subtitle must gate it on `!embedded`.

Common miss — a header whose title **falls back** to the app name: `const displayTitle = title || t('app.title')`. Gate the fallback (and a home page that passes the app name as `title`):

```tsx
const embedded = useEmbeddedInShell()
const displayTitle = embedded && (!title || title === t('app.title')) ? '' : title || t('app.title')
```

Hardcoded literals count too (`<h1>Sheet</h1>` in an app named Sheet), as do `<h3>` / `SectionHeading` list headings on home that just repeat the app name. Next.js: use the hook (`useSyncExternalStore`) — never read `window` during render.

- **Do not** remove the sticky header entirely — keep action slots, back, and dual-theme bar styling; only omit the **app name** text.
- Iframe detection is `window.self !== window.top`; it works on mobile browsers and the VTC native apps (shell loads child apps in an iframe there too). No query-param detection.

### Verify (App Builder / QA — required before publish)

1. **Static:** `~/cursor_rules/scripts/check-embedded-app-name.sh <app-dir>` → must print `PASS` (exit 0). Checks `@vtc/ui` lock version, home `pageTitle`/headings/subtitles that echo the app name, and custom headers without an embed guard (including `title || t('app.title')` fallbacks and case-insensitive `<h1–h3>` literals). A reviewed false positive on a **nested** or signed-out screen can be silenced with a `vtc-embed-ok` comment on that line or the line above — never on the home screen.
2. **Runtime:** open the app from `app.vtc.com/<module>` (or beta) at a **390×844 mobile viewport** → chrome bar shows the title; the iframe shows **no** text equal to the app name on the home screen (header or body). In DevTools on the iframe: `[...document.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,header *,main > p')].filter(e => e.textContent.trim().toLowerCase() === '<app name>'.toLowerCase())` → `[]`.
3. Open a nested screen → its screen title still shows.
4. Open the app URL **directly** in a top-level tab → header shows the app name (standalone); signed-out landing unchanged.
5. Rename the app in space Access settings → chrome title updates; child still shows no name.

## Responsive Layout Standard

Apps must be **mobile-first but responsive**. Do **not** force all authenticated screens into a 450px container.

On desktop, standard list screens must **not** be constrained to mobile width.

| Bad | Good |
|-----|------|
| List page centered in 450px on a 1920px monitor | List page at ~760–900px — comfortable reading, adequate spacing |

**Minimum viewport width:** 360px. All containers: `mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6`.

**Header and page body use the same max-width** for a given screen.

### Width by content type

| Tier | `max-width` | Tailwind | Use for |
|------|-------------|----------|---------|
| **Narrow forms** | 450px | `max-w-[450px]` | Settings, login-like flows, short forms, simple create/edit |
| **Reading** | 760px | `max-w-[760px]` | Articles, documentation, blog posts, long-form detail |
| **Standard CRUD** *(default)* | 900px | `max-w-[900px]` | Lists, admin screens, inventory, CRM, tasks, expenses, article listings, bookings, article editors |
| **Visual / grid** | 1100–1200px | `max-w-[1100px]` or `max-w-[1200px]` | Catalogs, portfolios, galleries, shops, property listings, card dashboards |

**Default authenticated screens:** `max-w-[900px]`. Use `max-w-[450px]` only when the screen is intentionally form-focused or phone-like.

```tsx
// Optional shared constant — src/lib/layout.ts
export const CONTAINER = {
  narrow: 'max-w-[450px]',
  reading: 'max-w-[760px]',
  standard: 'max-w-[900px]',  // default
  visual: 'max-w-[1200px]',
} as const
```

### Articles app

| Screen | Container |
|--------|-----------|
| Article list | `max-w-[900px]` |
| Article detail | `max-w-[760px]` |
| Article editor | `max-w-[900px]` |

## Sticky Header (App Shell)

Pass the **same container class** as the page body (`CONTAINER.standard`, etc.).

**Shell iframe embed:** omit app name — platform chrome shows it (`Platform shell chrome` above). Header left cluster is back-only when nested; action slots unchanged.

**Standalone:**

```tsx
<header className="sticky top-0 z-50 h-16 bg-white dark:bg-surface-800 border-b border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-700 shadow-sm">
  <div className={`h-full w-full ${CONTAINER.standard} mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3`}>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
      {showBack && <BackButton />}
      {!embedded && (
        <h1 className="text-xl font-bold text-app-accent dark:text-white truncate min-w-0">{appName}</h1>
      )}
    </div>

    <div className="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0">
      {slot1 && <HeaderSlot slot={1} {...slot1} />}
      {slot2 && <HeaderSlot slot={2} {...slot2} />}
      {slot3 && <HeaderSlot slot={3} {...slot3} />}
      <HeaderOverflowMenu items={overflowItems} />
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
```

- **Root / list home (embedded):** action slots only — no back, **no app name**
- **Root / list home (standalone):** app name on the left — no back button
- **Nested screens:** `BackButton` + (standalone only) app name — screen title goes in **page body**, not the top bar
- Long app names: `truncate`; do not hardcode `text-indigo-*` — use accent tokens
- **All screen actions** (create, save, search, settings, admin) live in the header slots — no bottom bar, no FAB

## Back button

Use on **nested / detail views only** — in the left header cluster. **Embedded:** back only (no app name after it). **Standalone:** immediately before app name. Not on list home.

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Size | `w-10 h-10` (40px touch target) |
| Shape | `rounded-xl` |
| Padding | `p-2` |
| Icon size | `w-5 h-5` |
| Position | **Standalone:** immediately before app name (`gap-2` in left cluster). **Embedded:** alone in left cluster when nested |
| Visibility | Only when nested / detail view |
| Hover | `hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-surface-700` |

```tsx
<button
  type="button"
  onClick={() => router.back()}
  aria-label={t('common.back')}
  title={t('common.back')}
  className="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 p-2 rounded-xl hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-surface-700 shrink-0"
>
  <BackIcon className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>
```

## Top bar — icons only (mandatory)

The sticky top bar is **icon-driven navigation**. Text belongs in page content, not the bar. **Do not let app developers pick arbitrary icons** — use **Header action slots** only.

| Zone | Allowed | Forbidden |
|------|---------|-----------|
| **Left** | **Embedded:** back icon when nested only. **Standalone:** app name (text) + back when nested | Screen titles, section headings, breadcrumbs with text labels; **embedded:** app name (chrome shows it) |
| **Right** | Up to **3 semantic slot icons** + **vertical ellipsis** (slot 4) | Arbitrary icons, text nav links, tabs, labeled buttons, bottom bars, FABs |

**Rules:**

- **Max 3 icons** in slots 1–3; everything else goes in the **slot 4 ellipsis menu**
- **Slot 4 is always** the vertical ellipsis (`MoreVertical`) on the **far right**
- Every top-bar action follows **Standard action icons** — `aria-label` + `title` from i18n
- **No text labels** in the top bar
- **No bottom action bar** — Save, Cancel, Create, Admin, Settings, Export, etc. use header slots or ellipsis menu
- **No FAB** — floating action buttons are forbidden; primary actions use **slot 1**
- Screen context (e.g. "Edit invoice", "Settings") → page body heading below the header, not in the bar

## Header action slots (platform-wide — mandatory)

Fixed positions so every VTC app feels consistent. Use the **platform icon set** — never invent one-off icons for standard actions.

| Slot | Position | Purpose | Platform icon | Examples |
|------|----------|---------|---------------|----------|
| **1** | 1st (left of group) | **Primary action** | `Plus` (create) · `Check` (save) · `ScanLine` (scan) | Add, New, Create, Save, Scan |
| **2** | 2nd | **Search or Filter** | `Search` · `ListFilter` | Search, Filter — pick **one** per screen, not both unless the other is in ellipsis |
| **3** | 3rd | **Context action** | `UserPlus` · `Share2` · `ShoppingCart` · `Calendar` · `Settings` | Invite, Share, Cart, Calendar, app-specific |
| **4** | **Always far right** | **Overflow menu** | `MoreVertical` | Admin, Settings, Export, Delete, duplicate, secondary actions |

**Slot rules:**

- Use **0–3** of slots 1–3 as needed — never more than 3 visible icons before ellipsis
- **Slot 4 is always present** on authenticated App Shell screens — even when slots 1–3 are empty, ellipsis holds settings/admin/overflow
- Map each app action to a slot — do not add a 5th header icon; put it in the ellipsis menu
- **List home:** slot 1 = Create, slot 2 = Search or Filter, slot 3 = app context, slot 4 = ellipsis (admin, settings, …)
- **Edit / create form:** slot 1 = Save (`Check`), slot 2/3 optional, Cancel via `BackButton`; Delete/Duplicate in ellipsis
- **Admin / settings gear** goes in the **ellipsis menu** by default — not a custom header icon unless slot 3 context warrants it
- Icons must come from the shared platform set (Lucide names above or `@vtc/ui` / `src/components/header/icons.ts`) — same glyph across all apps for the same semantic action

```tsx
// HeaderOverflowMenu — slot 4, always far right
<button
  type="button"
  aria-label={t('common.moreActions')}
  title={t('common.moreActions')}
  aria-haspopup="menu"
  aria-expanded={open}
  className="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[40px] min-h-[40px] p-2 rounded-xl text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-surface-700"
  onClick={() => setOpen(v => !v)}
>
  <MoreVertical className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>
{open && (
  <div role="menu" className="absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 min-w-[180px] rounded-xl border ... shadow-lg z-50">
    {overflowActions.map(action => (
      <button key={action.id} role="menuitem" className="w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm ...">
        {action.icon}
        <span>{action.label}</span>
      </button>
    ))}
  </div>
)}
```

## Standard action icons

Default pattern for **all top-bar icon actions** (create, filter, settings, ellipsis, etc.). Back button uses the same icon size and hover — see **Back button** for its fixed `w-10 h-10` sizing.

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Button size | `min-w-[40px] min-h-[40px]` |
| Padding | `p-2` |
| Shape | `rounded-xl` |
| Icon size | `w-5 h-5` |
| Color | `text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300` |
| Hover | `hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-surface-700` |
| Active / selected | `text-app-accent bg-app-accent/10` |

```tsx
const actionClass = (active = false) =>
  [
    'inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[40px] min-h-[40px] p-2 rounded-xl',
    'text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300',
    'hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-surface-700',
    active && 'text-app-accent bg-app-accent/10',
  ].filter(Boolean).join(' ')

<button type="button" aria-label={label} title={label} className={actionClass(isActive)}>
  <PlusIcon className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>
```

- Icons inherit color via `currentColor` — apply `text-*` on the button, not hardcoded fills on SVG paths

## Admin / settings gear

Admin and settings are **ellipsis menu items by default** — not a standalone header icon unless slot 3 context explicitly warrants it (e.g. settings-heavy app). When shown as slot 3, use the **Settings** icon from the platform set — same as **Standard action icons**; border emphasis only on visual-app public toolbars per brief.

## Header actions — icon-only (required)

All header actions are **icon-only** at every viewport width — no text labels in the top bar. Use **Standard action icons** classes.

```tsx
const [linkHref, setLinkHref] = useState(href)
useEffect(() => { setLinkHref(addTokenToUrl(href)) }, [href])

<Link
  href={linkHref}
  aria-label={label}
  title={label}
  className={actionClass(active)}
>
  <span className="inline-flex shrink-0 w-5 h-5">{icon}</span>
</Link>
```

- Apply `addTokenToUrl` **after mount** (`useState` + `useEffect`) — avoids hydration errors from JWT in `href`
- Inline SVG icons per action — `w-5 h-5`, `currentColor` fill/stroke; use **Header action slots** icons only
- Primary CTAs (Create, Save) use **slot 1** — never a bottom bar or FAB
- i18n: `label` from locale keys (accessibility via `aria-label` / `title` when icon-only)

## Runtime Accent Color Standard

All VTC apps must use **runtime accent CSS tokens** — never hardcoded `indigo-*`, `purple-*`, or per-app hex in components.

### How the shell passes theme to child apps

When a user opens an app from the **VTC shell** (personal or space context), the shell injects query parameters on the iframe URL. Child apps **cannot** read `app.vtc.com` / `app.posif.com` localStorage — they inherit branding **only from the URL** (and what they persist from that URL on first load).

| Param | Source | Child app use |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| `token` | Shell session JWT | Auth — `bootstrapAuthFromUrl()` |
| `user` | Active user id | Validate against JWT `user_id` |
| `group` / `g` | Active **space** id (`0` = personal) | Tenancy — `group_id` scope (`spaceScope.ts` / `getDbWithAuth`) |
| `mode` | User or space theme | `light` \| `dark` → `.dark` on `<html>` |
| `color` | **Space / network branding** | Runtime accent → `--app-accent*` tokens |
| `typography` | **Network branding policy** | `platform` \| `network` — app font policy |
| `font` | When `typography=network` | `system` \| `lato` → `--app-font-family` |
| `lang` | User locale | i18n provider |
| `tz` | User timezone preference (IANA) | Display times — `resolveUserTimeZone()` from `@vtc/client` ≥ 1.2.2 |

**User timezone (required for user-visible datetimes):** The shell Settings → General preference injects `tz` (e.g. `America/Sao_Paulo`). Child apps must:

1. Read `tz` from the URL and call `preserveThemeParams()` so it persists as `posif_tz` (`@vtc/client` ≥ **1.2.2**).
2. Format all user-visible datetimes with that IANA zone (`Intl` `timeZone` / equivalent). Fallback to the browser zone if `tz` is missing/invalid.
3. Listen for shell `THEME_SYNC` with `timezone` and update live (same path as `lang` / `mode`).
4. Keep storing/sending instants in **UTC / ISO** on the API — timezone is display (+ scheduling UI), not storage.

Do **not** show raw server-local or bare UTC strings to users when a shell timezone is available.

**Space color inheritance:** When the app is opened inside a **network space**, the shell sets `color` from that space's configured accent (network branding). The app must **not** override this with a fixed palette. Layout, surfaces, typography, and spacing stay platform-standard; **only accent** changes.

```
app.vtc.com (shell, space theme = #7C3AED)
  └─ iframe → vault.apps.vtc.com/?token=…&group=1205&mode=dark&color=%237C3AED&lang=en&tz=America/Sao_Paulo
                └─ ThemeProvider reads color → sets --app-accent* on documentElement
```

### Resolution order (accent color)

Apply in `LayoutContent.tsx` (or root client layout); pass result to `ThemeProvider`:

1. **`color` URL parameter** — shell-injected space/network branding (`?color=#7C3AED` or `?color=green`)
2. **`NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ACCENT`** — app publisher default (env, committed in `.env.production`)
3. **Persisted `posif_color`** — from `preserveThemeParams()` when client navigation drops query params
4. **Platform fallback — VTC Blue `#004A80`**

```tsx
// LayoutContent.tsx
const mode = searchParams.get('mode') ?? 'light'
const color =
  searchParams.get('color') ??
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ACCENT ??
  undefined // ThemeProvider → #004A80
const lang = searchParams.get('lang') ?? 'en'
const tz = searchParams.get('tz') // IANA; use resolveUserTimeZone() from @vtc/client

useEffect(() => {
  bootstrapAuthFromUrl()   // token, user, group
  preserveThemeParams()    // mode, color, lang, tz → localStorage
}, [])
```

`addTokenToUrl()` must **re-append** `token`, `group`, `mode`, `color`, `typography`, `font`, and `lang` on client navigation so space/network branding survives in-app links.

### CSS tokens (`ThemeProvider` + `globals.css`)

Set on `document.documentElement` at runtime (legacy v3: map in `tailwind.config`; v4: `@theme` block):

| Token | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `--app-accent` | Primary fill, app title, active states |
| `--app-accent-hover` | Hover on primary buttons |
| `--app-accent-soft` | Soft backgrounds, empty-state highlights |
| `--app-accent-border` | Accent borders, selected filter rings |
| `--app-accent-text` | Foreground accent on dark surfaces and soft accent backgrounds — **white in dark mode** |

`:root` in `globals.css` holds **fallbacks only** (VTC Blue `#004A80`). `ThemeProvider` overwrites them when `color` is present.

```css
:root {
  --app-accent: #004a80;
  --app-accent-hover: #003a6e;
  --app-accent-soft: color-mix(in srgb, var(--app-accent) 14%, transparent);
  --app-accent-border: color-mix(in srgb, var(--app-accent) 35%, transparent);
  --app-accent-text: var(--app-accent);
}

.dark {
  --app-accent-text: #ffffff;
}

@layer utilities {
  .dark .text-app-accent {
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .dark .text-app-accent-text {
    color: #ffffff;
  }
}
```

`ThemeProvider` must set runtime tokens including:

```ts
root.style.setProperty('--app-accent-text', mode === 'dark' ? '#ffffff' : accent)
```

Implement `applyAccentTokens()` in `src/lib/theme.ts` — normalize hex and named colors (`green`, `blue`, …), derive hover via darken/`color-mix`.

### Component rules

- **Do** use `bg-app-accent`, `text-app-accent`, `ring-app-accent`, `border-app-accent-border`, `bg-app-accent-soft`
- **Do** pair surfaces with `surface-*` / gray tokens — accent is for actions and emphasis, not page backgrounds
- **Do** support dual theme: every `text-app-accent` on a dark surface needs `dark:text-white`, `text-app-accent-text`, or the mandatory `globals.css` dark override — see **Dark mode accent contrast**
- **Do not** hardcode `#3B82F6`, `text-indigo-600`, `bg-indigo-600`, etc. in components
- **Do not** read parent shell localStorage for theme
- **Do not** add fallback accent hex in JSX — missing env/URL → `ThemeProvider` platform default

**Apply accent tokens to:** app title, primary buttons, active tabs, links, focus rings, selected filters, badges, loading indicators, empty-state highlights.

**Layout, spacing, cards, headers, forms, and dark mode stay platform-standard.** Only the accent hue changes per space or URL.

### Verify

- Open app from shell in a branded space → header/buttons match space `color`
- Open with `?color=#16a34a&mode=dark` → green accent fills/buttons; **titles, pills, and links remain readable** (white accent text on dark surfaces)
- Navigate via in-app links → `addTokenToUrl` preserves `color` and `group`
- No `color` param and no env → VTC Blue `#004A80`

## VTC Theme — Visual Identity

The VTC look comes from **consistent structure**, not a fixed color:

- Sticky app header — **standalone:** app name left; **shell embed:** no app name (platform chrome); **header action slots** (max 3 + vertical ellipsis); no bottom bar
- **Typography Standard** — platform type scale; no custom fonts per app
- Mobile-first **responsive** centered container
- Rounded cards
- Consistent forms
- Clear list / detail / edit patterns
- Dark mode support
- **Runtime accent color**

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Border radius | `rounded-xl` (12px) or `rounded-2xl` (16px) |
| Shadows | `shadow-md` / `shadow-lg` on cards & buttons |
| Borders | `border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-700` |
| Surfaces | `surface-*` slate tokens — not accent-colored |
| Accent | `--app-accent*` tokens — never hardcoded indigo/purple in components |
| Hover effects | `hover:shadow-lg` on cards & buttons |
| Destructive | `red-600` — semantic, not accent |

## Admin / Edit Page Layout

Use App Shell + this structure. Pick container tier by form complexity:

| Form type | Container |
|-----------|-----------|
| Settings, short/simple create/edit | `max-w-[450px]` |
| Standard CRUD editor, article editor | `max-w-[900px]` |

```tsx
<>
  <AppShellHeader
    slot1={{ icon: 'check', label: t('common.save'), onClick: handleSave }}
    overflow={[{ icon: 'trash-2', label: t('common.delete'), onClick: handleDelete }]}
    nested
    containerClass={CONTAINER.standard}
  />
  <main className={`${CONTAINER.standard} mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-6 text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300`}>
    <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6">{pageTitle}</h2>
    {/* Main form or editor — floating-label inputs */}
    <form>...</form>

    {/* Optional collapsible panels — assistant, metadata, advanced settings */}
    <CollapsiblePanel title={t('edit.assistant')}>...</CollapsiblePanel>
    <CollapsiblePanel title={t('edit.settings')}>...</CollapsiblePanel>
  </main>
</>
```

- Header: back (when nested) + (**standalone only** app name) + **slot 1 Save** + ellipsis (delete, settings, …); screen title in page body
- Body: single main form/editor column; side panels **collapsible** below or beside on wide layouts — not permanent sidebars
- **No bottom action bar** — Save in slot 1; Cancel via `BackButton`; secondary actions in ellipsis
- No `confirm()` on Cancel — explicit choice via back or ellipsis menu item

## Public Content / Detail Page Layout

Articles, posts, catalog items, case studies — clean **reading** layout (`max-w-[760px]`):

```tsx
<main className="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-6 pb-16">
  {/* Top action row — share, edit (icon), back */}
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">...</div>

  {/* Hero media when relevant */}
  {coverUrl && (
    <img src={coverUrl} alt="" className="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover mb-6 shadow-md" />
  )}

  <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{title}</h2>
  {subtitle && <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">{subtitle}</p>}
  <div className="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">
    {author && <span>{author}</span>}
    {tags?.map(tag => (
      <span key={tag} className="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-app-accent-soft text-app-accent-text text-xs font-medium">{tag}</span>
    ))}
  </div>
  <article className="mt-6 prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none">{body}</article>
