```

- Reading-first: generous vertical rhythm, no nested cards around body copy
- Top action row: icon buttons aligned right (or `BackButton` left + actions right)
- Hero media: full container width, `rounded-2xl`, only when the entity has cover/image
- Long-form with embedded wide media/tables: may use `max-w-[900px]` when the brief requires it

## Buttons (All Must Have Visible Backgrounds)

Use accent tokens for primary actions — not hardcoded indigo/purple.

```tsx
{/* Primary */}
<button className="px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium bg-app-accent hover:bg-app-accent-hover text-white rounded-xl shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all">

{/* Secondary */}
<button className="px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium rounded-full bg-gray-200 dark:bg-surface-700 text-gray-700 dark:text-surface-200 hover:bg-gray-300 dark:hover:bg-surface-600 transition-colors">

{/* Destructive — semantic red, not accent */}
<button className="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-700 text-white rounded-xl shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all">
```

**Do not use FABs** — primary create/add actions use **header slot 1** (`ui.mdc`).

## Floating Label Inputs (All Inputs Must Use This)

Use **`@vtc/ui`** — do not copy-paste field markup into each app:

```tsx
import { FloatingInput, FloatingTextarea, FloatingSelect } from '@vtc/ui'

<FloatingInput
  id="name"
  label={t('form.name')}
  value={name}
  onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
  required
  error={errors.name}
/>

<FloatingTextarea id="notes" label={t('form.notes')} value={notes} onChange={...} rows={5} />

<FloatingSelect id="status" label={t('form.status')} value={status} onChange={...}>
  <option value="open">{t('status.open')}</option>
</FloatingSelect>
```

| Prop | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `id` | Required — ties label to control |
| `label` | Floated label text (i18n) |
| `required` | Shows red `*`; pass to native control |
| `error` | Inline message + `aria-invalid` + red border |
| `labelSurface` | `default` \| `panel` — label notch background when nested in a tinted panel |

Raw markup (only if `@vtc/ui` cannot be used):

```tsx
<div className="relative">
  <input
    type="text"
    id="fieldName"
    value={value}
    onChange={handleChange}
    placeholder=" "
    className="peer w-full px-4 py-3 border border-surface-300 dark:border-surface-600 rounded-xl focus:ring-2 focus:ring-app-accent focus:border-app-accent dark:bg-surface-700 dark:text-white bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
  />
  <label
    htmlFor="fieldName"
    className="absolute left-4 top-3.5 text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400 transition-all duration-200 pointer-events-none bg-white dark:bg-surface-800 px-1
      peer-focus:-top-2.5 peer-focus:text-xs peer-focus:text-app-accent-text
      peer-[:not(:placeholder-shown)]:-top-2.5 peer-[:not(:placeholder-shown)]:text-xs peer-[:not(:placeholder-shown)]:text-surface-600"
  >
    Label {required && <span className="text-red-500">*</span>}
  </label>
</div>
```

- ✅ `placeholder=" "` (single space) is required for the float effect
- ✅ Active: prominent accent border + ring (`ring-app-accent`)
- ✅ Inactive: thin light grey border

